{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"76184c81-fca8-48f4-a78f-e166313baccc","step_index":7,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"results\":[],\"stub\":true,\"stub_explanation\":\"No vulnerability was found in this flow. In `ERC721.safeTransferFrom(address,address,uint256,bytes)`, `transferFrom` passes `auth = _msgSender()` to `Raffle._update` and `ERC721._update`, which loads `from = _ownerOf(tokenId)` and enforces `_checkAuthorized(from, auth, tokenId)` before any state mutation or external receiver callback. For unminted or burned tickets (`from == address(0)`), `_tokenApprovals[tokenId]` and `_operatorApprovals[address(0)]` are always cleared/empty and `auth != address(0)`, so `_isAuthorized` returns false and `_checkAuthorized` reliably reverts with `ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId)`. For existing tickets where `_msgSender()` is neither the owner, an approved operator, nor the token-approved address, `_checkAuthorized` reliably reverts with `ERC721InsufficientApproval(spender, tokenId)`.\"}\n","duration_seconds":18.743814,"usage":{"input_tokens":3813,"output_tokens":1288,"thinking_tokens":1042,"cache_read_tokens":27428,"total_tokens":5101}}}
